    <bpmn:process id="W_W61" name="W61. Competitor Price Match Process" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests price match at POS based on competitor&#x27;s current advertised price
Frequency: ~50–100 price match requests/day chain-wide; ~2–5 per store per week
Volume: Primarily on high-visibility items (power tools, paint, appliances, tiles) where customers actively compare prices
Owner: Cashier (execution); Store Manager (authorization)
Participants: Cashier, Store Manager, Pricing Analyst (review)
Source: workflow W61 — Competitor Price Match Process</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W61_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W61_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W61_Lane2" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W61_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W61_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W61_Lane5" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W61_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W61_Start7" name="Customer requests price match at POS based on competitor&#x27;s current advertised price">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W61_Task8" name="Customer requests price match at checkout; presents competitor price proof (ad…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer requests price match at checkout; presents competitor price proof (ad, screenshot, catalog)
Responsible (R): Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: —</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W61_Task9" name="Cashier verifies eligibility per policy rules: (a) competitor is on eligible…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cashier verifies eligibility per policy rules: (a) competitor is on eligible list, (b) item is identical (brand, model, size), (c) proof is current (within 7 days), (d) quantity within limit
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W61_Task10" name="Cashier enters price override in POS with reason code &quot;Competitor Price Match&quot;…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Cashier enters price override in POS with reason code &quot;Competitor Price Match&quot;; system prompts for competitor name and matched price; if override &gt; 10% or &gt; PHP 500: manager authorization required per W5B.4a
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W61_Task11" name="If matched price is below BuildRight&#x27;s cost (WAC): system blocks override and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If matched price is below BuildRight&#x27;s cost (WAC): system blocks override and alerts Store Manager; Store Manager contacts Category Manager for authorization; Category Manager may approve as strategic decision (customer retention, competitive response) with written justification in system
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W61_Task12" name="System records price match transaction: original price, matched price…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System records price match transaction: original price, matched price, competitor name, cashier ID, authorizer ID, item, quantity, and reason code (W5B.4a audit trail)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W61_Task13" name="Weekly: Pricing Analyst reviews price match report: frequency by SKU…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Weekly: Pricing Analyst reviews price match report: frequency by SKU, competitor, and store; identifies items with high price match frequency (&gt; 5 requests/week) for potential SRP adjustment (W40) or competitive response strategy
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W61_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W61_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W61_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W61_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-278 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Support &amp; Complaints (PA-13.1).) | - operational: must track these as deliberate margin concessions
Owner: Cashier (execution); Store Manager (authorization)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
