    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W328" name="W328. Customer Credit Limit Periodic Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual credit review calendar (every 12 months from account opening or last review); or triggered early by material adverse event (payment default &gt; 60 days, significant order volume increase, negative trade reference)
Frequency: Annual for all trade/corporate accounts (~5,400 accounts); ad-hoc for adverse events (~100–200 early reviews/year)
Volume: ~5,200 annual reviews ÷ 12 months = ~430 reviews/month; peaks at fiscal year-end when batch reviews are scheduled
Owner: Credit Analyst
Participants: Credit Analyst, Finance Manager, AR Clerk, Sales Rep, Customer (trade/corporate account holder)
Source: workflow W328 — Customer Credit Limit Periodic Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W328_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W328_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W328_Lane2" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W328_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W328_Start4" name="Annual credit review calendar (every 12 months from account opening or last review); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W328_Task5" name="Batch review scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Batch review scheduling: System generates annual credit review list each month — accounts due for review (12 months since last review or opening date); system ranks by exposure (highest outstanding balance + open orders first)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Credit Analyst
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W328_Task6" name="Automated risk scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated risk scoring: System computes updated risk score per account using: (a) payment behavior (average days-to-pay, number of late payments in last 12 months, days sales outstanding trend), (b) credit utilization (outstanding balance ÷ current limit, trend), (c) order volume trend (current year vs. prior year), (d) any collection escalations in last 12 months (W108 history), (e) any credit memo/debit memo disputes (W70 history); system classifies accounts as Green (low risk), Yellow (moderate risk), Red (high risk)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W328_Task7" name="Green accounts — streamlined review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Green accounts — streamlined review: Credit Analyst reviews Green-flagged accounts (typically 70–80% of batch); if risk score is stable and no adverse indicators, Analyst approves continuation of existing credit limit with notation; no customer contact required
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 5 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W328_Task8" name="Yellow accounts — enhanced review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Yellow accounts — enhanced review: Credit Analyst pulls updated financial information: (a) requests latest financial statements or bank certification from customer, (b) checks trade references, (c) reviews order and payment history in detail; Analyst prepares credit assessment memo with recommendation: maintain, increase, or decrease limit
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W328_Task9" name="Red accounts — full review and action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Red accounts — full review and action: Credit Analyst conducts full credit reassessment: (a) pulls financial statements, trade references, and bank certifications, (b) evaluates if credit limit should be reduced, placed on hold, or revoked, (c) prepares recommendation with supporting evidence; Finance Manager reviews and decides
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W328_Task10" name="Limit adjustment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Limit adjustment: If limit changes: (a) system updates credit limit in customer master (W253), (b) system generates customer notification letter stating new limit and effective date, (c) Sales Rep informed of limit change to manage customer relationship, (d) if limit reduced: system flags any open orders exceeding new limit for Sales Rep review
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W328_Task11" name="Ad-hoc early review trigger">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Ad-hoc early review trigger: If a material adverse event occurs between scheduled reviews (e.g., customer payment default &gt; 60 days, customer reported in financial distress, significant order volume spike &gt; 200% of average): system flags account for immediate credit review outside the annual cycle; Credit Analyst initiates steps 4 or 5 as appropriate
Responsible (R): System / Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W328_Task12" name="Batch completion and reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Batch completion and reporting: At month-end, Credit Analyst produces credit review summary: number of accounts reviewed, limit changes (increases/decreases), accounts placed on hold, total exposure change; Finance Manager reviews and signs off; report feeds into W35 management reporting
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W328_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W328_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
