    <bpmn:process id="W_W597" name="W597. Customer Complaint Escalation Matrix &amp; Resolution SLA Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer complaint received via any channel (in-store, call center, social media, email, website) and classified by severity
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 complaints/month chain-wide; escalation varies by severity — Severity 1 (critical): ~50–80/month, Severity 2 (high): ~300–400/month, Severity 3 (medium): ~800–1,200/month, Severity 4 (low): ~800–1,200/month
Volume: Channels: in-store (~40%), call center (~25%), social media (Facebook, Instagram — ~15%), email/web form (~15%), chat (~5%); complaint types: product quality (30%), pricing errors (20%), service delays (20%), staff behavior (15%), safety incidents (5%), other (10%); DTI-reportable complaints: ~30–50/year
Owner: Customer Service Manager
Participants: CSR, CS Manager, Store Manager (R/A for in-store), Call Center Agent, Social Media Manager, VP Store Operations (A for Severity 1), Legal Counsel (A for DTI-escalated), HR Manager (I for staff behavior complaints), Department Head (I for product issues)
Source: workflow W597 — Customer Complaint Escalation Matrix &amp; Resolution SLA Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W597_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W597_Lane1" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W597_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W597_Lane3" name="CS Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W597_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W597_Start5" name="Customer complaint received via any channel (in-store, call center, social media, email…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task6" name="Complaint intake and classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Complaint intake and classification: complaint received via any channel — (a) in-store: CSR creates ticket at customer service counter with details, photos of product/issue, and customer contact; (b) call center: agent creates ticket during call with recording reference; (c) social media: Social Media Manager creates ticket from Facebook comment/DM/Instagram mention with screenshot and public URL; (d) email/web: system auto-creates ticket from email/form submission; (e) chat: agent creates ticket from live chat transcript; system captures: ticket number, channel, customer info (loyalty lookup or guest), complaint category (product quality, pricing error, service delay, staff behavior, safety incident), description, supporting evidence (photos, receipts, order number); CSR/agent assigns initial severity based on classification matrix above
Responsible (R): CSR / Call Center Agent / Social Media Mgr
Accountable (A): CS Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W597_Task7" name="SLA clock starts">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: SLA clock starts: system starts SLA timer upon ticket creation — (a) first response SLA timer starts immediately; (b) resolution SLA timer starts simultaneously; (c) system sends automated acknowledgment to customer with ticket number and expected response time (channel-appropriate: SMS for in-store, email for web, reply for social media); (d) SLA timers visible on ticket dashboard with countdown and color coding: green (&gt;50% SLA remaining), amber (25–50%), red (&lt;25%), black (breached)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task8" name="First response per SLA">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: First response per SLA: assigned agent provides first response — (a) acknowledge complaint and validate customer concern; (b) confirm understanding of issue (repeat back to customer); (c) for Severity 1: CS Manager personally responds within 30 min with action plan; for social media Severity 1: public response within 30 min (&quot;We take this seriously and are investigating — our team will contact you directly within the hour&quot;); (d) for Severity 2: CS Manager or designated senior agent responds within 2 hours; (e) for Severity 3–4: CSR/call center agent responds within SLA with initial assessment and next steps; (f) first response logged in ticket with timestamp and SLA compliance recorded
Responsible (R): CSR / CS Manager
Accountable (A): CS Manager
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task9" name="Resolution attempt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Resolution attempt: agent executes resolution per complaint type — (a) product quality: arrange exchange (W12), warranty claim (W33), or refund per return policy; (b) pricing error: verify pricing discrepancy, process refund for overcharge, escalate to W553 if systemic pricing error; (c) service delay: check delivery/service status per W19/W138, arrange expedited resolution, issue service recovery voucher; (d) staff behavior: document complaint, escalate to HR Manager for investigation (confidential), provide customer with assurance of corrective action; (e) safety incident: isolate product if applicable, escalate to W512 (store H&amp;S committee), document for insurance, immediate notification to VP Store Operations and Legal; (f) resolution proposal communicated to customer with specific remedy
Responsible (R): CSR / CS Manager
Accountable (A): CS Manager
Duration: 10–30 min (Severity 3–4); 30–60 min (Severity 2); continuous (Severity 1)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W597_Task10" name="Escalation if unresolved per matrix">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Escalation if unresolved per matrix: if resolution cannot be achieved within the assigned SLA — (a) Severity 3–4 approaching SLA breach: ticket auto-escalates from CSR to CS Manager with 25% SLA remaining; CS Manager takes over resolution; (b) Severity 2 approaching SLA breach: ticket escalates from CS Manager to Store Manager (if store-specific) or VP Store Operations (if chain-wide); (c) Severity 1: continuous escalation chain — every 30 min without resolution, escalation advances one level (CS Manager → VP Store Operations → Legal → COO); (d) social media Severity 1–2: Social Media Manager monitors public thread, provides updates every 2 hours until resolution, escalates to VP Marketing if negative engagement exceeds threshold; (e) all escalations logged with timestamp, reason, and new responsible party
Responsible (R): System / CS Manager
Accountable (A): Per escalation matrix
Duration: 2 min per escalation action</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task11" name="DTI-reportable complaint flag">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: DTI-reportable complaint flag: for complaints that may require DTI reporting — (a) system flags complaints matching DTI criteria: product safety hazard, misleading advertising, non-compliance with product standards, refusal to honor warranty, price tag discrepancy per the Consumer Act (RA 7394) price-tag and labeling rules; (b) CS Manager reviews flagged complaints within 4 hours; (c) if DTI-reportable: CS Manager notifies Legal Counsel immediately; Legal Counsel assesses whether to (i) proactively file report with DTI (demonstrates good faith), or (ii) resolve directly with customer and document resolution; (d) all DTI-flagged complaints tracked in separate register for annual DTI compliance audit; (e) if customer files DTI complaint: Legal Counsel manages response per W469 (DTI consumer adjudication board process); (f) maintain complaint log per the company&#x27;s consumer-compliance policy (Art. 164 sanctions apply to confirmed Consumer Act violations)
Responsible (R): CS Manager / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 15–30 min per flagged complaint</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task12" name="Resolution confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Resolution confirmation: agent confirms resolution with customer — (a) customer agrees to proposed resolution; (b) system executes financial actions: refund processing, voucher issuance, exchange order creation; (c) agent closes ticket with resolution code: (i) full refund, (ii) exchange/replacement, (iii) partial refund/credit, (iv) service recovery (voucher/discount), (v) apology and explanation (no financial action), (vi) escalated to legal/DTI; (d) resolution timestamp recorded for SLA compliance tracking
Responsible (R): CSR / CS Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W597_Task13" name="CSAT survey">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: CSAT survey: upon ticket closure, system triggers CSAT survey — (a) in-store: QR code on printed receipt linking to survey; (b) call center: IVR survey at end of call or SMS survey link; (c) social media/email/web: survey link in resolution confirmation message; (d) survey: overall satisfaction (1–5 scale), was issue resolved? (Y/N), would you recommend BuildRight? (0–10 NPS); (e) CSAT data feeds into W65 customer satisfaction measurement and W507 root cause analysis; (f) for Severity 1–2: CS Manager reviews CSAT response personally and follows up if score &lt;3
Responsible (R): System / CS Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 min (system) + 5 min per low-score follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task14" name="Complaint analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Complaint analytics: weekly, CS Manager generates complaint analytics dashboard — (a) volume by severity, category, channel, and store; (b) SLA compliance: first response SLA compliance % and resolution SLA compliance % by severity; (c) escalation rate: % of tickets escalated beyond initial tier; (d) resolution type distribution; (e) CSAT by severity and channel; (f) top 10 stores by complaint volume per 1,000 transactions; (g) top 10 SKUs generating complaints; (h) DTI-flagged complaint status summary; (i) social media complaint sentiment trend; dashboard shared with VP Store Operations, Category Managers, and Store Managers weekly
Responsible (R): CS Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task15" name="Monthly SLA performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Monthly SLA performance review: CS Manager presents monthly SLA performance to VP Store Operations and Department Heads — (a) SLA compliance targets: Severity 1 first response 100%, resolution 95%; Severity 2 first response 98%, resolution 90%; Severity 3 first response 95%, resolution 85%; Severity 4 first response 90%, resolution 80%; (b) actual vs. target by severity; (c) chronic SLA breach categories (categories with &lt;80% compliance for 2+ months); (d) escalation effectiveness: % of escalated complaints resolved within extended SLA; (e) DTI compliance status: open DTI cases, resolved cases, DTI penalties incurred; (f) corrective action plan for underperforming categories; (g) feed into W507 for systemic root cause analysis
Responsible (R): CS Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W597_Task16" name="Quarterly DTI compliance audit preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: Quarterly DTI compliance audit preparation: CS Manager compiles quarterly DTI compliance documentation — (a) complaint log per the consumer-compliance policy: all complaints received, resolution, time to resolution; (b) DTI-flagged complaint register: status and resolution for each; (c) pricing accuracy documentation (cross-reference W553); (d) product safety incident log (cross-reference W512); (e) warranty compliance documentation (cross-reference W33); (f) consumer information compliance (price tags, product labeling per the Consumer Act RA 7394 IRR); documentation stored for 3-year retention per DTI requirements
Responsible (R): CS Manager
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W597_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W597_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W597_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W597_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-278 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Support &amp; Complaints (PA-13.1).) | - operational: 30-minute first response SLA for social media Severity 1, pre-approved response templates, and escalation to VP Marketing for viral events; operational: proactive resolution before DTI escalation, maintaining detailed complaint logs per RA 7394, and demonstrating good-faith resolution attempts; operational: remote CS Manager support, phone-based escalation, and relaxed resolution SLA for stores &gt;100 km from regional office (+50% resolution SLA extension)
Owner: Customer Service Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W597_Assoc19" sourceRef="W597_Annotation18" targetRef="W597_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
