    <bpmn:process id="W_W707" name="W707. Omnichannel Returns &amp; Refund Orchestration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer initiates return via any channel: in-store POS, ecommerce website, mobile app, customer service hotline; or automated return trigger (damaged in delivery, wrong item shipped)
Frequency: Daily; ~93,000 POS transactions/day with ~2% return rate (per profile §5); ~1,400 ecommerce orders/day with ~10–12% return-request rate (the W1623 canon)
Volume: ~1,860 POS returns/day + ~130–170 ecommerce return requests/day (≈ 4,000–5,000/month per W1623, of which the ≈ 3,300–4,200/month store drop-offs flow through W12B/W1273; the remainder ≈ 800–1,700/month is refunded on courier pickup per W215) ≈ ~2,000 total returns/day across all channels
Owner: Customer Service Manager
Participants: Store Associate (in-store returns), Ecommerce Operations (online returns), DC Returns Team (W651 reverse logistics), AR Clerk (refund processing), Customer Service Rep (hotline/chat returns)
Source: workflow W707 — Omnichannel Returns &amp; Refund Orchestration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W707_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W707_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W707_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W707_Lane3" name="Store Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W707_Lane4" name="Customer Service Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W707_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W707_Start6" name="Customer initiates return via any channel: in-store POS, ecommerce website, mobile app…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W707_Task7" name="Return initiation (channel-agnostic)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Return initiation (channel-agnostic): customer initiates return through any channel: (a) in-store: customer brings item and receipt to Customer Service counter; (b) ecommerce: customer logs into website/app, selects order and items to return, selects reason (defective, wrong item, changed mind, not as described, damaged in delivery), chooses return method (in-store drop-off or courier pickup); (c) hotline/chat: Customer Service Rep creates return request on customer&#x27;s behalf; (d) system validates: order exists, return is within policy window (POS: 14 days with receipt; ecommerce: 30 days), item is returnable category (exclusions: cut lumber, mixed paint, installed items per W169, W170)
Responsible (R): Customer / Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Customer Service Manager
Duration: 5-10 min per return request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W707_Task8" name="Return authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Return authorization: system creates Return Authorization (RA): (a) unique RA number linked to original order (POS transaction number or ecommerce order number); (b) RA specifies: items, quantities, return reason, refund method options, return routing (in-store → W12 process, courier pickup → DC reverse logistics per W651); (c) for BORIS (buy-online-return-in-store): system flags RA as cross-channel, enabling store to process return against ecommerce order; (d) for BOPIS returns: same as BORIS if order was placed online; (e) system generates QR code or RA number for tracking
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Customer Service Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W707_Task9" name="In-store return processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: In-store return processing: for returns presented at store: (a) Store Associate scans item barcode and RA QR code; (b) system validates: item matches RA, item condition (resalable, damaged, defective); (c) if resalable: accept return, item goes back to selling floor or backroom inventory; (d) if damaged/defective: accept return, item routed to damage processing per W91/W92; (e) for BORIS: system reconciles against ecommerce order (not store inventory), routes item to DC for restocking or disposition per W651; (f) Store Associate processes refund per step 5
Responsible (R): Store Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10-15 min per return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W707_Task10" name="Ecommerce courier return processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Ecommerce courier return processing: for online returns via courier: (a) system generates prepaid return shipping label (partner courier per W668 delivery network); (b) customer packages item and schedules pickup or drops at courier location; (c) courier delivers returned item to DC; (d) DC Returns Team receives and inspects item per W651; (e) DC updates return status in system: received, inspected, condition assessment; (f) system triggers refund processing per step 5
Responsible (R): Customer / Courier / DC Returns Team
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 3-7 days transit + 15-30 min inspection</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W707_Task11" name="Refund processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Refund processing: system processes refund based on original payment method and channel: (a) credit card refund: initiate refund to original card (3-5 business days for bank processing); (b) e-wallet refund (GCash, Maya): initiate refund to original wallet (1-2 business days); (c) cash refund (in-store only): issue cash from register per W66 cashiering process; (d) store credit / gift card: issue electronic store credit valid 12 months; (e) refund amount: full refund if defect/damage/wrong item; restocking fee (10-15%) for change-of-mind on non-defective items; (f) for BORIS: refund debited from ecommerce entity, credited from store entity per intercompany settlement W87; (g) system updates AR subledger and customer account
Responsible (R): System / Store Associate / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Automated (electronic) or 5 min (cash)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W707_Task12" name="Cross-channel inventory reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Cross-channel inventory reconciliation: system performs real-time inventory reconciliation for cross-channel returns: (a) BORIS return: inventory added to DC (not store) since item belongs to ecommerce inventory pool; (b) ecommerce return to DC: inventory added to DC for restocking or disposition; (c) intercompany inventory transfer for BORIS: system auto-generates intercompany transfer order per W87; (d) weekly: Finance reconciles cross-channel return journal entries
Responsible (R): System / Finance
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Automated + 4 hours/week reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W707_Task13" name="Return analytics &amp; policy optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Return analytics &amp; policy optimization: monthly, Customer Service Manager analyzes return data: (a) return rate by channel (POS vs. ecommerce), by category, by reason; (b) BORIS adoption rate (% of ecommerce returns processed in-store); (c) refund method distribution; (d) average time from return initiation to refund completion by channel; (e) restocking fee revenue vs. processing cost; (f) identify products with &gt;10% return rate for quality investigation per W110; (g) feed findings into Merchandising (product quality), Operations (packaging improvements), and Customer Service (policy refinement)
Responsible (R): Customer Service Manager
Accountable (A): Head of Customer Service
Duration: 4-6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W707_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W707_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W707_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W707_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-278 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Support &amp; Complaints (PA-13.1).) | - operational: return history tracking per customer per CRM-030 and threshold alerts; operational: blocks and staff training
Owner: Customer Service Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W707_Assoc16" sourceRef="W707_Annotation15" targetRef="W707_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
