    <bpmn:process id="W_W783" name="W783. Customer Credit Application Scoring &amp; Risk Assessment Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New B2B customer credit application per W24; or annual credit review per W328
Frequency: ~100–150 new credit applications per month; ~430 annual reviews/month (per W328: ~5,200 annual reviews ÷ 12)
Volume: ~100–150 new applications + ~430 annual reviews = ~530–580 credit assessments/month
Owner: Credit Analyst
Participants: Credit Analyst, Sales Manager, Finance Manager, Customer
Source: workflow W783 — Customer Credit Application Scoring &amp; Risk Assessment Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W783_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W783_Lane1" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W783_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W783_Lane3" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W783_Lane4" name="Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W783_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W783_Start6" name="New B2B customer credit application per W24; or annual credit review per W328">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W783_Task7" name="Application intake and completeness check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Application intake and completeness check: Credit Analyst receives application: (a) Business registration documents (SEC/DTI registration, BIR Certificate of Registration per REG-001), (b) Financial statements (audited FS for corporate accounts, tax returns for sole proprietorships), (c) Trade references (minimum 3 suppliers), (d) Bank references, (e) Authorized signatories with specimen signatures, (f) BIR Form 2303 (Certificate of Registration)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W783_Task8" name="Business verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Business verification: Credit Analyst verifies: (a) SEC/DTI registration via online verification, (b) BIR TIN validity per W732, (c) business permit validity per W54 LGU compliance, (d) Google Maps/store visit verification for physical existence, (e) negative news search (litigation, bankruptcy, fraud)
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30-60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W783_Task9" name="Quantitative credit scoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quantitative credit scoring: System computes credit score using weighted model: (a) Financial health (40%): revenue, profitability, liquidity ratios, debt-to-equity from submitted FS, (b) Payment history (25%): BuildRight payment track record for existing customers per W108, trade reference feedback, (c) Business stability (20%): years in operation, business registration type, ownership structure, (d) Industry risk (10%): construction/developer risk weighting per FIN-060 sector analysis, (e) Relationship value (5%): projected annual purchases from application
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Credit Analyst
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W783_Task10" name="Credit limit recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Credit limit recommendation: Based on credit score: (a) Score ≥ 80 (Low Risk): recommended limit = 10% of projected annual purchases or PHP 5M, whichever is lower, (b) Score 60-79 (Medium Risk): recommended limit = 5% of projected annual purchases or PHP 2M, whichever is lower, (c) Score 40-59 (Higher Risk): recommended limit = PHP 500K with Net 15 COD terms, (d) Score &lt; 40 (High Risk): decline with recommendation for COD-only account per W24
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W783_Task11" name="Credit terms determination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Credit terms determination: Based on score and limit: (a) Net 30 for Low Risk, (b) Net 30 for Medium Risk with 10% retention per delivery, (c) Net 15 for Higher Risk, (d) COD for High Risk/declined, (e) special terms (Net 60/90 for government/institutional per W78) require Head of Trade / Account Management approval
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W783_Task12" name="Approval workflow">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Approval workflow: (a) Credit limit ≤ PHP 500K: Credit Analyst recommends, Finance Manager approves, (b) PHP 500K–2M: Finance Manager recommends, CFO approves, (c) &gt; PHP 2M: CFO recommends, CEO approves, (d) annual review with limit increase &gt; 25%: escalates one approval level
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO / CEO
Duration: 10 min/review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W783_Task13" name="Customer notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer notification: Approved: (a) customer receives credit agreement per W688 contract management, (b) payment terms and credit limit communicated, (c) account activated in customer master per W253. Declined: (a) Sales Manager communicates decision with alternative options (COD, reduced terms), (b) customer may reapply after 6 months with updated financials
Responsible (R): Sales Manager / Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W783_Task14" name="Continuous monitoring setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Continuous monitoring setup: Approved account enters continuous monitoring per W572: (a) automated Amber/Red alerts configured, (b) trade reference refresh at 6 months, (c) first annual review scheduled per W328
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W783_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W783_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W783_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W783_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-278 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Support &amp; Complaints (PA-13.1).) | - operational: Credit Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Credit Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W783_Assoc17" sourceRef="W783_Annotation16" targetRef="W783_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
