    <bpmn:process id="W_W1521" name="W1521. Customer Verified Contractor &amp; Installer Referral Directory Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests contractor/installer recommendation; quarterly contractor directory refresh cycle; contractor complaint or performance issue
Frequency: ~800–1,200 directory-governance actions/month across 200 stores (the directory layer; transaction-level matchmaking runs per W904 at ~1,500–2,000 requests/month); quarterly directory audit
Volume: ~300–500 verified contractors/installers in directory across all trade categories
Owner: Service Coordinator Lead
Participants: Service Coordinator Lead, Category Managers, Store Managers, accredited contractors/installers, Customer
Source: workflow W1521 — Customer Verified Contractor &amp; Installer Referral Directory Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1521_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1521_Lane1" name="Service Coordinator Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1521_Lane2" name="Service Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1521_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1521_Start4" name="Customer requests contractor/installer recommendation; quarterly contractor directory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1521_Task5" name="Contractor recruitment and application">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Contractor recruitment and application: (a) Service Coordinator Lead recruits contractors through: (i) existing BuildRight installation subcontractors who also take private jobs, (ii) walk-in contractor inquiries at store service counters, (iii) local contractor association referrals, (iv) trade professional customers (plumbers, electricians, tile setters) identified through trade account purchases; (b) contractor submits application with: (i) business name and DTI/SEC registration, (ii) trade-specific licenses/certifications (PRC license for engineers, TESDA NC-II for electricians/plumbers, TESDA RAC NC II for aircon technicians), (iii) portfolio of completed projects with photos, (iv) 2–3 customer references, (v) proof of general liability insurance
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator Lead
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30–60 min/application review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1521_Task6" name="Verification and background check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Verification and background check: (a) Service Coordinator Lead verifies: (i) PRC/TESDA license validity and currency via online verification, (ii) business registration with DTI/SEC, (iii) calls 2–3 references and documents feedback, (iv) checks for any BuildRight customer complaints against the contractor (cross-reference W795 installation complaint data); (b) if verification passes: contractor added to directory with trade categories, service area (km radius from stores), and contact information; (c) if verification fails: contractor rejected with explanation of missing credentials
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator Lead
Accountable (A): Store Manager (local market)
Duration: 1–2 hours/contractor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1521_Task7" name="Customer referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer referral (in-store): (a) customer requests contractor recommendation at service counter; (b) Service Coordinator queries directory by: (i) trade category (electrician, plumber, tile setter, carpenter, painter, general contractor, structural engineer, architect), (ii) geographic proximity to customer&#x27;s site, (iii) customer rating (4+ stars preferred), (iv) availability; (c) provides customer with 2–3 contractor options: name, trade, phone number, star rating, brief description of specialties; (d) important disclaimer: &quot;BuildRight verifies credentials but does not employ or guarantee these contractors. Customer contracts directly with the contractor. BuildRight is not liable for contractor workmanship or pricing.&quot;
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1521_Task8" name="Customer feedback collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer feedback collection: (a) after referred contractor completes a job, Service Coordinator contacts customer (SMS or in-store follow-up): (i) did the contractor perform satisfactorily?, (ii) 1–5 star rating, (iii) would you recommend this contractor to others?, (iv) any issues or complaints?; (b) system logs feedback against contractor profile; (c) if complaint: investigate per W795 if workmanship issue; if behavioral/ethical issue: flag contractor for review
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator / System
Accountable (A): Service Coordinator Lead
Duration: 5–10 min/referral</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1521_Task9" name="Quarterly directory audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly directory audit: (a) Service Coordinator Lead reviews all contractors in directory: (i) average customer rating (remove contractors below 3.5 stars), (ii) license/certification expiry dates (remove or suspend contractors with expired credentials), (iii) activity level (inactive &gt; 6 months: contact for renewal or remove), (iv) complaint volume (2+ unresolved complaints in quarter: suspend pending investigation); (b) updates directory: add new contractors, remove/suspend underperformers, update contact information and service areas; (c) publishes updated directory to store service counters and BuildRight website/app
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator Lead
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1521_Task10" name="Contractor dispute resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Contractor dispute resolution: (a) if customer files complaint against referred contractor: (i) Service Coordinator Lead documents complaint, (ii) contacts contractor for their response, (iii) mediates resolution if possible (rework, partial refund), (iv) if resolution fails: advises customer of their legal options, (v) flags contractor in directory — multiple unresolved complaints trigger suspension; (b) BuildRight does not accept financial liability for contractor work; mediation is a goodwill service
Responsible (R): Service Coordinator Lead
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–3 hours/dispute</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1521_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1521_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1521_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1521_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-278 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Support &amp; Complaints (PA-13.1).) | - operational: Service Coordinator Lead review and approval gate
Owner: Service Coordinator Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1521_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1521_Annotation12" targetRef="W1521_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow14" sourceRef="W1521_Start4" targetRef="W1521_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow15" sourceRef="W1521_Task5" targetRef="W1521_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow16" sourceRef="W1521_Task6" targetRef="W1521_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow17" sourceRef="W1521_Task7" targetRef="W1521_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow18" sourceRef="W1521_Task8" targetRef="W1521_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow19" sourceRef="W1521_Task9" targetRef="W1521_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1521_Flow20" sourceRef="W1521_Task10" targetRef="W1521_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1521_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1521_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1521">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_End11_di" bpmnElement="W1521_End11"><dc:Bounds x="1680" y="317" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1521_Annotation12_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Annotation12"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="460" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1450" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1630" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1680" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1521_Assoc13_di" bpmnElement="W1521_Assoc13"><di:waypoint x="340" y="460" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1550" name="W1550. Customer Voice-of-Customer (VOC) Monthly Analysis, Trend Dashboard &amp; Strategic Insight Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly VOC analysis cycle (1st week of month for prior month data)
Frequency: Monthly
Volume: Aggregation across all customer feedback channels — POS CSAT (~300K–400K responses/month at the 10–15% response rate), ecommerce reviews (~2K/month), call center surveys (~5K/month), social media mentions (~10K/month), NPS quarterly surveys (~15K responses)
Owner: Customer Experience Manager
Participants: Customer Experience Manager, Data Analyst, VP Marketing, VP Store Operations, Category Managers
Source: workflow W1550 — Customer Voice-of-Customer (VOC) Monthly Analysis, Trend Dashboard &amp; Strategic Insight Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1550_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1550_Lane1" name="Data Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1550_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1550_Lane3" name="Customer Experience Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1550_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1550_Start5" name="Monthly VOC analysis cycle (1st week of month for prior month data)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1550_Task6" name="Multi-channel data aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Multi-channel data aggregation: Data Analyst extracts customer feedback data from all sources — POS CSAT scores by store/department/cashier, ecommerce product ratings and review text, call center CSAT and resolution scores, social media sentiment scores (positive/neutral/negative), NPS scores and verbatim comments; consolidates into unified VOC dataset
Responsible (R): Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Customer Experience Manager
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1550_Task7" name="Text analytics &amp; topic extraction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Text analytics &amp; topic extraction: System applies NLP text analytics to verbatim feedback — extract recurring topics/themes (e.g., &quot;long queue&quot;, &quot;product out of stock&quot;, &quot;delivery late&quot;, &quot;friendly staff&quot;, &quot;good quality&quot;); sentiment scoring per topic; identify emerging topics not seen in prior months
Responsible (R): System / Data Analyst
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1550_Task8" name="Trend analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Trend analysis: Data Analyst compares current month vs. prior month and vs. same month prior year — overall satisfaction score trend, NPS trend, topic frequency changes, store-level heatmap (bottom 20 stores by CSAT), category-level sentiment (which product categories generate most negative feedback)
Responsible (R): Data Analyst
Accountable (A): Customer Experience Manager
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1550_Task9" name="Strategic insight synthesis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Strategic insight synthesis: Customer Experience Manager synthesizes analysis into monthly VOC Insight Report — top 5 positive themes, top 5 negative themes, top 3 emerging risks, recommended actions (with responsible team and deadline); examples: &quot;Tile category complaint rate increased 40% due to breakage in transit → Packaging review with W1546 vendor audit&quot;; &quot;South Luzon stores underperforming on CSAT → W67 store performance review&quot;
Responsible (R): Customer Experience Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1550_Task10" name="Executive VOC dashboard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Executive VOC dashboard: System generates interactive VOC dashboard — overall satisfaction score, NPS, topic word cloud, store heatmap, category sentiment chart, trend lines; accessible to C-suite and VP-level via mobile and desktop
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1550_Task11" name="Action item distribution &amp; tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Action item distribution &amp; tracking: Customer Experience Manager distributes specific action items to responsible teams — merchandising (product quality issues), store operations (service issues), supply chain (availability issues), ecommerce (platform issues); tracks action item completion in closed-loop system (W87)
Responsible (R): Customer Experience Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1550_Task12" name="Quarterly deep dive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly deep dive: Every quarter, Customer Experience Manager conducts deeper analysis — customer segment comparison (B2C vs. B2B vs. trade), loyalty tier analysis, competitor benchmark (where data available), correlation analysis (satisfaction vs. spend vs. churn); presents to executive team
Responsible (R): Customer Experience Manager
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1550_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1550_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1550_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1550_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-278 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Support &amp; Complaints (PA-13.1).) | - operational: Customer Experience Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Customer Experience Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
